foreign  [Music]  shows off his dance moves on Sister  Wives  [Music]  I'm just a guy who just doesn't hold  back the Brown family patriarch takes a  solo road trip to attend his pal Brian's  wedding in Oklahoma and because he's  officiating he's breaking his strict  coveted rules I decided to stop checking  covid numbers it seems like it's safe to  sort of poke my head out I am feeling  like it's time to sort of emerge from  all this quarantining the sequester that  we've had with coven but Cody doesn't  quite feel prepared to officiate mostly  because his marriage with Christine just  ended my thoughts so far about marriage  ironically have been mixed  and it's crazy that I'm here performing  this wedding he was questioning whether  he was the best guy to talk at a wedding  when he was struggling so much in his  relationship he would bring that up  often with me in conversation because he  feels like it's a little bit of a  failure that he that this this marriage  is falling apart the timing for me to  leave was just it opened up and  everything became just things fell into  place so well but despite being nervous  Cody follows through and MC's the ideas  each others being a standard  he does a pretty good job and he doesn't  says things that other people only wish  they could and while the wedding looked  great fans are zoning in on one thing  when he busted a move at the reception  [Music]  that's the crowd circling around Cody  then at one point he dances with a  fellow guest  [Music]  but while Cody's having a good time  Janelle and Christine get a little  heated taking offense to his decision to  hit up a wedding after he refused to see  them and their kids amid the pandemic I  see Christine and I see Mary and I see  Janelle and I see Robin all of them  based upon uh essentially their behavior  regarding the outside world you know  because of covet 19. yeah the travel  choice is interesting to me and I  realize it's important but Cody and  Robin still observed the very strict  rules about covid and yet here's Cody  traveling are you gonna mask up while  you're officiating are they going to  have to follow Cody's no that's  ridiculous they're not going to have to  follow Cody's rules but the one thing  that really infuriates Christine how  Cody made an exception to go to a  wedding but chose to skip their daughter  Isabelle's surgery  Isabelle's heartbroken she goes how can  he justify officiating Brian's wedding  when he wouldn't even come to my surgery  and now I'm mad what the hell you think  you gotta go officiate your friend's  wedding and not take care of your own  family you know it's hard it's difficult  but I work hopefully going to be fine  you know I think I was a lot more  optimistic that we would be like besties  so I'm not quite sure about that but  we'll see but then Cody explains there  was a bigger reason behind it Isabel's  surgery was at a time and a situation  where it would have required that I am  six or eight weeks away from home no man  could be away from work and from home  and from family that long  I was gone for four days for Brian's  wedding the lack of love between us was  for a reason  so glad I'm not because I cannot respect  this person anymore fast forward to  present day and Christine's happy live  in that single life that's more like a  personal strength that I feel like I  have more than I've ever felt before  because I was able to make steps for my  future and for my present and so I just  feel more confident as well and while  the TLC star is not yet ready for a new  relationship she tells ET the quality  she's looking for in her next partner  kindness  real just kindness a romantic  relationship for sure someone who's  attracted to me would be a really great  thing I'm just saying so yeah all of  that  [Music]

